name 'ai-and-algorithmic-decisions-preassessment-q2_2026'

question 'A clothing store adds a "Try It On" feature where a shirt color updates the moment you tap a swatch. Why is this a good example of user-centered design?'

wrong 'It uses the newest framework available.'
wrong 'It hides complexity from developers so they can code faster.'
right 'It gives users instant feedback so they can see the result of their choice without waiting.'
wrong 'It saves the user from typing the color name.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

